  "body": {
    "id": "lem:allocation-reflection",
    "kind": "lemma",
    "statement": "After optimization over common channels and confidence rules, complete randomization with \\(m\\) treated units and with \\(N-m\\) treated units have the same minimax expected-cardinality value.",
    "free_symbols": [
      "N",
      "m"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "ass:fixed-population",
      "ass:binary-outcomes",
      "ass:complete-randomization",
      "ass:common-channel",
      "ass:conditional-product",
      "ass:pure-local-privacy",
      "def:confidence-lp"
    ],
    "proof_tex": "Map an assignment to \\(W'_i=1-W_i\\), a schedule to \\(Y'_i(0)=Y_i(1)\\), \\(Y'_i(1)=Y_i(0)\\), and permute a channel's four input rows by \\((w,y)\\mapsto(1-w,y)\\).  Complete randomization sends \\(m\\) treated units bijectively to \\(N-m\\) treated units and preserves the uniform mass.  Row permutation preserves every local-privacy inequality, the common-channel property, and the conditional product.  Moreover\n\\[\n \\tau(s')=\\frac1N\\sum_i\\{Y_i(0)-Y_i(1)\\}=-\\tau(s).\n\\]\nReflect every reported confidence set by \\(A\\mapsto-A\\).  Coverage probabilities and cardinalities are unchanged.  The construction is an involution, so it gives inequalities in both directions and therefore equality of the two optimized values.",
